  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "NNN people ordered NNN takeouts at the same place. The arrival time of the ithi^{th}ith takeout is XiX_iXi​, and the arrival time of the ithi^{th}ith person is YiY_iYi​ where Xi&lt;YiX_i &lt; Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​.\n\nAlso X1&lt;X2&lt;…&lt;XNX_1 &lt; X_2 &lt; \\ldots &lt; X_NX1​&lt;X2​&lt;…&lt;XN​ and all Xi,YiX_i, Y_iXi​,Yi​ values are distinct (i.e. Xi≠XjX_i \\ne X_jXi​=Xj​ for all i,ji, ji,j; Yi≠YjY_i \\ne Y_jYi​=Yj​ for all i,ji,ji,j; Xi≠YjX_i \\ne Y_jXi​=Yj​ for all i,ji,ji,j).\n\nOriginally, everyone could happily get their own takeout, but a demon appeared. The demon can steal **exactly** 111 takeout.\n\nThe demon knows the regular pattern of human action. When a person arrives for the takeout:\n\n\nIf his takeout exists, he will happily take his takeout;\nIf his takeout does not exist, and there are other takeouts, (because he is dazed by anger) he will take the takeout with the lowest number;\nIf there is no takeout, he can only leave in frustration.\nDefine **evil person** as the person who takes the takeout that does not belong to him. The demon wants to maximize the number of **evil people**. Can you help him?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the number of people\nThe next line contains NNN numbers X1,X2,…,XNX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_NX1​,X2​,…,XN​ where XiX_iXi​ denotes the arrival time of ithi^{th}ith takeout\nThe next line contains NNN numbers Y1,Y2,…,YNY_1, Y_2, \\ldots, Y_NY1​,Y2​,…,YN​ where XiX_iXi​ denotes the arrival time of ithi^{th}ith person\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the maximum number of **evil people** people.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Xi&lt;Yi≤2N1 \\leq X_i \\lt Y_i \\leq 2N1≤Xi​&lt;Yi​≤2N",
      "all Xi,YiX_i ,Y_iXi​,Yi​ values are distinct (i.e. Xi≠XjX_i \\ne X_jXi​=Xj​ for all i,ji, ji,j; Yi≠YjY_i \\ne Y_jYi​=Yj​ for all i,ji,ji,j; Xi≠YjX_i \\ne Y_jXi​=Yj​ for all i,ji,ji,j).",
      "X1&lt;X2&lt;…&lt;XNX_1 \\lt X_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt X_NX1​&lt;X2​&lt;…&lt;XN​",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
